# Q everywhere: IC16's input 3B (CH6_N) is stuck high, so the load gate no longer tells a character from a control code: the HALT ($76) that ends each row of the display file loads a glyph too, the one of code $36, Q. Every empty place on the screen is a Q, and the margins, where the ROM's running code is loaded as dots, fill up as well.
machine bw80
title "Q everywhere"
brief "The BW-80 works, but every empty place on the screen is filled with the letter Q, and the margins around the picture are full of junk. What is typed shows over the Qs."
fault stuck IC16.3B 1
